  "id": "COMPOUND:15061 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "Chaxamycin B appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and (1S,2R,7R,9S,10S)-6-acetyl-6'-methoxy-1'-methylspiro[4-oxa-12-azatricyclo[7.2.1.02,7]dodec-5-ene-10,3'-indole]-2'-one. These compounds all lead to the activation of SK-VLB, suggesting a potential mechanism where the sialyltransferase is a critical mediator in the signaling pathway that ultimately results in SK-VLB activation. The evidence indicates that Chaxamycin B may act by modulating this enzyme, thereby influencing SK-VLB activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the sialyltransferase in the biological response to Chaxamycin B, with SK-VLB being a downstream effector of this enzymatic interaction.",
